-- lib/mem/rc11.cub — the language-level memory model: RC11 consistency (Lahav, Vafeiadis, Kang,
-- Hur, Dreyer, "Repairing sequential consistency in C/C++11", PLDI 2017) for the five orderings
-- of lib/mem/atomics.cub, over the events and witness of lib/isa/tso.cub. Loaded after
-- lib/mem/atomics.cub.
--
-- A language-level candidate execution is a `TsoX` (events, rf, the order on writes: RC11's
-- mo is its restriction to each location) with the ordering of each event (`modes`, by event
-- id). An update (exchange, successful compare-exchange) is ONE event that reads and writes
-- (kind k-L), so RC11's rmw relation is the identity on such events: `rf ; rmw` is rf into an
-- update, and atomicity is irreflexivity of rb ; mo.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- relations as lists of pairs
RcRel : Type
RcRel = List (Word × Word)
